---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import trust from '../../config/release-trust.json';
import { defaultRecipient } from '../generated/default-recipient';
---

<Layout title="Security">
  <h1>Security boundaries</h1>
  <p>
    No reviewed release is available. Tests and restrictive browser policies do
    not establish a cryptographic proof or audit.
  </p>
  <p>
    A malicious host can replace delivered JavaScript. Before sensitive use,
    verify a pinned local sender through an independently trusted channel. A
    same-site hash or badge does not establish trust.
  </p>
  <h2>Confirm the recipient</h2>
  <p>
    Check the complete SHA-256 public-key fingerprint with the recipient using
    an existing trusted contact. A filename, badge or value shown by this site
    cannot establish identity on its own. If the operator holds the default
    recipient's private key, the operator can decrypt ciphertext you choose to
    share with them; messages are not automatically delivered to them.
  </p>
  <p>
    The sender displays the full fingerprint and requires an explicit checkbox
    before encryption. That checkbox records your confirmation that you made the
    comparison; it is not an automated identity check, and the site does not
    label a key verified based on parsing or your acknowledgment.
  </p>
  {defaultRecipient && (
    <p class="fingerprint">
      Configured public recipient: {defaultRecipient.name} · RSA-
      {defaultRecipient.bits}
      <br />
      SHA-256: {defaultRecipient.fingerprint}
    </p>
  )}
  <h2>Verify code before sensitive typing</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Obtain the exact official origin and reviewed release hashes through an
      independently trusted publisher channel. Bookmark that origin; avoid
      search ads and unsolicited download links.
    </li>
    <li>
      For a local HTML sender, compare the complete file's SHA-256 outside the
      file before opening it. The page cannot verify itself.
    </li>
    <li>
      For the Windows receiver, require the expected full hash, a Valid
      Authenticode signature and the exact expected certificate Subject. Any
      signature alone is insufficient. Stop on mismatch or missing evidence; do
      not bypass operating-system warnings.
    </li>
    <li>
      Confirm the recipient separately. Release-signing credentials and
      recipient RSA keys serve different purposes.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A valid signature proves provenance relative to the trusted publisher;
    review still matters. TLS authenticates domain control, and a clone can copy
    all visible text, logos and hashes. There is no automatic clone detector.
  </p>
  <dl>
    <dt>Official HTTPS origin</dt>
    <dd>
      {trust.officialOrigin ??
        'Pending operator confirmation; no official release origin established.'}
    </dd>
    <dt>Proposed Vercel address</dt>
    <dd>
      {trust.proposedOrigin} — pending availability, deployment and
      response-header verification.
    </dd>
    <dt>Expected Windows signing publisher</dt>
    <dd>
      {trust.expectedAuthenticodePublisher ??
        'Pending; no signed receiver release available.'}
    </dd>
    <dt>Independent release-verification channel</dt>
    <dd>
      {trust.independentVerificationChannel ??
        'Pending; same-site downloads and hashes do not close this gap.'}
    </dd>
    <dt>Reviewed release</dt>
    <dd>
      {trust.reviewedRelease ??
        'Pending integrated independent review and final artifact hashes.'}
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <h2>Cryptographic and device limits</h2>
  <p>
    RSA provides neither forward secrecy nor post-quantum security. Browser
    strings, extensions, operating systems and exported files remain outside
    guaranteed erasure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The envelope reveals approximate plaintext byte length. Public-key
    encryption supplies no sender authentication. This implementation has no
    formal IND-CCA2 proof, FIPS certification or government approval, and makes
    no constant-time JavaScript claim. Public transcription checks are not
    authentication. Read{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/">what stays in memory and what exports persist</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
